@startuml rendering-system
!theme plain
skinparam classStyle rectangle
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam defaultFontName Arial

title DOM Rendering System

package "DOM Rendering (Vue Composable)" #LightBlue {
  class useCellRenderer {
    - cellPool: Map<string, HTMLElement>
    - cellSize: Ref<number>
    ---
    + renderCell(coord: Coordinate, container: HTMLElement): void
    + removeCell(coord: Coordinate): void
    + clearAllCells(): void
    + updateCellSize(size: number): void
    - getOrCreateCell(key: string): HTMLElement
    - returnCellToPool(key: string, element: HTMLElement): void
  }

  class "Map<string, HTMLElement>" as CellPool {
    Flyweight pattern
    Reusable DOM elements
    ---
    Key: "row,col"
    Value: <div> element
  }
}

package "Browser APIs" #white {
  class HTMLElement <<external>> {
    + style: CSSStyleDeclaration
    + classList: DOMTokenList
  }

  class "DOM Container" as Container <<external>> {
    Grid container element
  }
}

' Relationships
useCellRenderer *-- CellPool : manages pool
useCellRenderer ..> HTMLElement : creates/reuses
useCellRenderer ..> Container : appends to

note right of useCellRenderer
  **Flyweight Pattern:**

  Reuses DOM elements from pool
  instead of creating/destroying
  on every render cycle

  Benefits:
  - Reduces GC pressure
  - Faster rendering
  - Smoother animations

  **Vue Composable:**

  Returns reactive refs and methods
  for use in Vue components
end note

note right of CellPool
  **Pool Management:**

  When cells are removed from the grid,
  their DOM elements are kept in the
  pool instead of being destroyed.

  When new cells need to be rendered,
  elements are reused from the pool.

  This avoids the cost of:
  - createElement()
  - appendChild()
  - DOM reflows
end note

note bottom of useCellRenderer
  **Rendering Flow:**

  1. renderCell(coord, container)
     - Check if cell exists in pool
     - If yes: reuse element
     - If no: create new element
     - Update position (top, left)
     - Add to container

  2. removeCell(coord)
     - Find cell element
     - Hide or remove from DOM
     - Return to pool for reuse

  3. updateCellSize(size)
     - Update all cell dimensions
     - Recalculate positions
end note

note left of HTMLElement
  **Cell Element Structure:**

  <div class="cell"
       style="
         position: absolute;
         top: {row * cellSize}px;
         left: {col * cellSize}px;
         width: {cellSize}px;
         height: {cellSize}px;
       ">
  </div>

  Positioned absolutely within
  the grid container.
end note

@enduml
